{"agent":"adp-census2","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The baseline format writes raw TAB-separated fields without escaping. A valid POSIX path such as `ddflow/foo\\tbar.py` is recorded by `format_baseline` with an embedded tab; `parse_baseline` then does `kind, family, path, n = raw.split(\"\\t\")`, receives five fields, and raises `ValueError` (a newline in a path similarly corrupts `splitlines()`). The ratchet therefore cannot round-trip its own baselines for valid filesystem names.","digest":"c76911d1eb81f739","location":"ddflow/services/archifaces.py:format_baseline, parse_baseline","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/archifaces.py:format_baseline, parse_baseline"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`_git_hooks_join` is invoked for every `ast.Call` and flattens any call's positional arguments, but it never checks that the call is `os.path.join`, `Path`, or any path constructor. Given `logger.debug(\".git\", \"hooks\")` or `fake(\".git\", \"hooks\")`, the scanner emits a `managed-file` site for `.git/hooks`, although no managed file is referenced. This is a false dependency and can make the arch guard fail on a false positive.","digest":"47f89988cffc9ded","location":"ddflow/services/archifaces_scan.py:_git_hooks_join","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/archifaces_scan.py:_git_hooks_join"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"Managed-file detection runs on every non-prose string literal before URL classification and does not skip URL strings. A literal like `\"https://example.com/settings.json\"` produces both a `network` site and a `managed-file` site with family `settings.json`. A URL path component is not a local file owned by another tool, so this is a false `managed-file` dependency.","digest":"6e7798470b11cd42","location":"ddflow/services/archifaces_scan.py:_literal_site","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/archifaces_scan.py:_literal_site"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"For shell-invocation strings, only `e.value.split()[0]` is used. Given `os.system(\"git status && pre-commit run\")`, the scanner records only `program` family `git` and misses `pre-commit`, a second external program run by the same command. This underreports interfaces and defeats the “every external interface” census for compound shell commands.","digest":"2a5574404ed482bb","location":"ddflow/services/archifaces_scan.py:program_of","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/archifaces_scan.py:program_of"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`os.environ[\"FOO\"] += \":x\"` is an environment-variable read: augmented assignment invokes `__getitem__` before `__setitem__`. In that AST, the `Subscript` parent has `ctx=ast.Store`, so `_environ` enters its `Subscript` branch but skips recording because it only records when the `ctx` is `ast.Load`. The scanner therefore fails to count this environment read.","digest":"05b0596374c24e91","location":"ddflow/services/archifaces_scan.py:_environ","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/archifaces_scan.py:_environ"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`file_protocols` is built from every `ast.Constant` method string, including `self.prose` docstrings/bare string statements. A docstring/statement exactly equal to `\"tools/list\"` will make an unrelated real `\"jsonrpc\"` literal be recorded as `protocol mcp`, so a docstring can change the emitted site despite the intent that docstrings/string statements cannot produce or influence hits.","digest":"842d4e55fad0a311","location":"ddflow/services/archifaces_scan.py:_Scan.run","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/archifaces_scan.py:_Scan.run"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The round-trip assertion compares `I.parse_baseline(text)` with `I.parse_baseline(I.format_baseline(c))`, where `text` is already `I.format_baseline(c)`; since `format_baseline(c)` is deterministic, this is just `x == x`. It would still pass if `format_baseline` discarded every site and `parse_baseline` returned an empty census, so the test does not verify a census survives `parse(format(census))` and the ratchet has no actual round-trip guard.","digest":"52b0648ff67984a2","location":"tests/test_arch_interfaces.py:test_baseline_format_round_trips_and_names_no_values","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_arch_interfaces.py:test_baseline_format_round_trips_and_names_no_values"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"`test_real_tree_ratchet_against_committed_baseline` calls `I.scan(ROOT)`, which scans the entire repository root including test directories and potentially untracked or user-specific files. Because it is sensitive to the exact file layout and contents of the working directory, running the test suite in a dirty workspace or an environment with extra untracked files will cause this test to fail spuriously due to unexpected interface call sites or ratchet drift.","digest":"1fdbe0a28bef2d8c","location":"tests/test_arch_interfaces.py:279","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_arch_interfaces.py:279"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":50729,"diff_sha":"7e2e5029333afeecc7ee42d6d1f0fc225830f6a4baafb1212991b62f4dc140f5","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1221.9,"excluded_bytes":1015,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr"],"family":"deepseek","findings":8,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"7b816600cfc0f8c8","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/ADP-census-v2.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261101T230908Z-218236a0.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewed_head":"be1c01dd6d522e4d5f0eff2074be34daa7c54d6b","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/arch_deps.py":"100644 442cab9aa22bef2bf32d0d13e3e98b1ef3d359bf","ddflow/services/archifaces.py":"100644 c4ac8dd7c8f7c0d832807a8a0cc106d92aed5265","ddflow/services/archifaces_scan.py":"100644 8b71793fb5e6c9a1af0c86